WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.610
Apple is the most valuable publicly traded
company in the world.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:08.940
And Elon Musk hasn’t shied away from trying to take another bite out of the company.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.539
The drama surfaced when Wall Street Journal
reporter Tim Higgins came out with a book

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:15.459
about Tesla that included a wild claim.

00:00:15.459 --> 00:00:19.500
That Elon Musk tried to replace Tim Cook as
Apple’s CEO.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.210
According to the book, at the height of Tesla’s
problems with mass-producing its most affordable

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:28.980
vehicle, the Model 3, in 2016, Cook suggested
to Musk that Apple buy Tesla, at which point

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.276
Musk lobbied to take over Cook’s job.

00:00:31.276 --> 00:00:35.379
Cook is said to have angrily hung up the phone
but not before unleashing an expletive.

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:36.379
(F*&amp; you).

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:39.079
Both men have denied the conversation 
took place.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:42.649
This is what Cook told the New York Times’
Kara Swisher on her podcast Sway:

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:47.940
“You know, I’ve never spoken to Elon,
although I have great admiration and respect

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.149
for the company he’s built.”

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:52.910
Musk made the point of saying they’ve “...never
spoken or written to each other ever.”

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:57.039
However, he admitted that during Tesla’s
toughest days, he did request a meeting with

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:00.379
Cook to talk about the prospect of Apple acquiring
Tesla.

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:02.290
But there weren’t any conditions involved.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.670
Musk went on to say that Cook “refused to
meet” with him.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.729
And added at the time, Tesla was
worth only 6 per cent of its current valuation.

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:13.200
Who knows what an Apple acquisition might
have looked like. After all, Musk isn’t

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.750
exactly the company’s biggest fan.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.360
During Tesla’s second-quarter earnings call,
he made a point of saying Apple uses more

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.479
cobalt than Tesla does.

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:25.540
Some cobalt mined in conflict areas like the
Congo has been linked to child labor.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.170
And the mining process has been blamed for
devastating the environment.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:34.875
It is, however, the key ingredient in lithium-ion
batteries that power iPhones and electric cars.

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:39.180
Tesla has since announced it’s starting
to shift toward cobalt-free iron phosphate

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.550
(LFP) batteries instead.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.170
For Apple’s part, it has said its long-term
goal is to not mine cobalt at all, but rather,

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:48.540
recycle old iPhones and recover cobalt for
re-use.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.630
Musk has snipped at Apple many times.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:56.049
For example, in response to Apple kicking
Fortnite off the App Store for violating Apple’s policies.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:02:00.440
The game’s developer, Epic Games, had tried
to get around Apple’s 30% cut of App Store

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.700
revenue by implementing its own in-app payment
system.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.770
Epic is now suing Apple for its meaty cut
of revenue.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.440
Musk showed his support for Epic by tweeting:
“Apple app store fees are a de facto global

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.860
tax on the internet.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.010
Epic is right.”

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.748
He’s spoken out about what he feels is Apple’s
anti-competitive behavior.

00:02:17.748 --> 00:02:21.945
“Our goal is to support the advent of sustainable
energy.

00:02:21.945 --> 00:02:27.525
It is not to create a walled garden and use
that to bludgeon our competitors, which is

00:02:27.525 --> 00:02:29.695
sometimes used by some companies.

00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:32.390
(Cough) Apple (cough).”

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.160
Musk appeared to fake a cough and mutter “Apple.”

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.230
Turns out, the two companies could soon be
directly competing with one another.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:43.920
Apple has reportedly been quietly developing
an autonomous electric vehicle since 2014

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.980
that is meant to give Tesla a run for its money.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:50.860
Though Musk appeared to write it off early
on, telling the German newspaper Handelsblatt

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.880
in 2015: “It’s good that Apple is moving
and investing in this direction.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.780
But cars are very complex compared to phones
or smartwatches.”

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.100
But Cook doesn’t see a self-driving car
as anything but technology.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.140
Though he’s played coy about what exactly Apple
has in the works.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.390
Would it be in the form of a car or the technology
within a car?

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.560
I’m not going to answer that question.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.790
Apple is well known for keeping things under
tight wraps.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.670
It has reportedly held talks with several
car companies about teaming up to build an

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.340
electric car though it’s apparently still
searching for a partner.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.750
So an electric Apple car - if it ever appears
- could still be years away.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.700
Musk doesn’t think Apple has the right people
to get it done, saying it has hired people

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:37.880
Tesla has fired, likening Apple to a graveyard
filled with those who couldn’t cut it at Tesla.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:42.170
But then he appeared to dial back the criticism,
clarifying: “I don’t hate Apple.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.070
I'm glad they're doing an EV.”

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:47.870
Whether Apple ends up coming out with a car
or not, it’s already well known as one of

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.830
the most transformative companies in history.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:55.570
Apple has created an ecosystem where its devices
are designed to work seamlessly with one another

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.660
which entices fans to buy them all.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.700
In this regard, it appears as if Musk is trying
to take a page out of Apple’s book.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.770
Tesla is now looking to expand its own ecosystem
by going beyond cars.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:08.890
It already offers solar roofs for homes that
generate energy that can be stored in a Tesla

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.940
powerwall that can power your house when the
grid goes down.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:14.250
The powerwall can also charge your Tesla.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:19.850
And your car can be covered by Tesla’s own
insurance, just like Apple Care covers Apple products.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.820
The Tesla ecosystem seems to be ever-expanding.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.600
Musk has said he’s keen to develop a Tesla
HVAC system - a heating, ventilation, and

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.130
air conditioning system, bringing the tech
developed from its cars into homes.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:37.610
The entrepreneur believes the key to a successful
company lies in its ability to rapidly innovate

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.710
and create heart-stopping products.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.534
He thinks that Apple used to wow the world,
but not anymore, as he once told Kara Swisher.

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:48.470
“Apple used to really bring out products
that would blow peoples’ minds, you know?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.984
And they still, make great products, but there's
less of that.

00:04:52.984 --> 00:04:56.080
I don't think people are necessarily running
to the store for the iPhone 11.”

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.380
Still, it hasn’t stopped Musk from continuing
to use his very own Apple iPhone.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.940
Anyone who's bought shares in either Apple
or Tesla and has held them for long enough

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.670
is reaping the rewards.

